(* GHOST direct messages: attribution forward secrecy as key erasure (design faza9-dm.md §6.3
   P-7, §14.1 T34, §21.3 point 6; obligation M-7 of §9.5; slice S13).

   P-7: for an ISO week w with now >= start(w + 1) + 45 d, no key on either device and nothing
   derivable from either seed opens or recognises a pair-mode envelope of week w. The mechanism is
   erasure plus one-wayness: a root is random (never derived from a seed) and is erased once K_b
   exists; K_{w+1} = HKDF(K_w, "pair-next") is one-way; a week key is erased with its recognition
   key (R-S6) once its window closes. A seizure after that finds only later week keys.

   The model: a week-w envelope with its recognition hint (the attribution handle: whoever holds
   R_sel(K_w) can tell the envelope belongs to this conversation), then the ratchet walks six weeks
   and the live week's envelope goes out; phase 1 is the seizure, which gets the one week key
   still stored. The erased week key is a private free name so that its secrecy is the query:
   whoever cannot derive K_w can neither open nor recognise week w, since R_sel is a one-way
   function of it. The seed-derived values the seizure also gets (card keys, namespaces) are not
   inputs to any of these derivations (T26), so they are left out. Expected results are in
   expected.txt; msgLive is the control that the seizure does read what is still live.

   Declared limits: this is key secrecy standing in for unlinkability (an equivalence property is
   future work), and the skipped Olm message keys of live sessions (§7.7 point 4, pruned at 51 d)
   and provisional reply seeds (§6.7) are outside it; the T34 world measures those. *)

free c: channel.

type key.

fun knext(key): key.
fun recog(key): key.
fun hint(key, bitstring): bitstring.
fun seal(bitstring, key): bitstring.
reduc forall m: bitstring, k: key; unseal(seal(m, k), k) = m.

(* K_w of the erased week, derived from a root that is itself erased (random, never seed-derived). *)
free kWeekW: key [private].
free msgWeekW: bitstring [private].
free msgLive: bitstring [private].

query attacker(kWeekW).
query attacker(msgWeekW).
query attacker(msgLive).

process
  new salt: bitstring;
  new saltLive: bitstring;
  let kLive = knext(knext(knext(knext(knext(knext(kWeekW)))))) in
  (
    (* week w: the envelope and its recognition hint go to the relay *)
    out(c, (salt, hint(recog(kWeekW), salt), seal(msgWeekW, kWeekW)))
  | (* six weeks later, under the live week key *)
    out(c, (saltLive, hint(recog(kLive), saltLive), seal(msgLive, kLive)))
  | (* the seizure, after week w's key was erased: the live week key is all that is stored *)
    phase 1; out(c, kLive)
  )
